        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): use boundary-aware home path replacement in chrome-mcp diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`redactChromeMcpDiagnosticTextWithLocalPaths` in `extensions/browser/src/browser/chrome-mcp.ts` uses `text.split(homePath).join(\"~\")` to redact home paths from diagnostic text — the same naive split/join pattern that was fixed in #98876 (`packages/terminal-core/src/display-string.ts`). This corrupts sibling paths that share the home prefix.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe `split().join()` pattern matches the home directory as a substring anywhere in the text. When a sibling path like `/home/user2/project` appears in diagnostic output alongside the real home path `/home/user`, both get corrupted to `~2/project` instead of preserving the sibling.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers with home directories that are a prefix of another path (e.g., `/home/user` vs `/home/user2`) see corrupted diagnostic output in browser MCP log messages.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real behavior proof — reproduced via node:**\n```\nInput:  \"Error in /home/user2/project: file not found at /home/user/config.json\"\nOLD:    \"Error in ~2/project: file not found at ~/config.json\"  <- sibling corrupted\nNEW:    \"Error in /home/user2/project: file not found at ~/config.json\"  <- fixed\n```\n\n**Validation:**\n- tsgo typecheck: passed\n- `pnpm test extensions/browser/src/browser/chrome-mcp.test.ts`: 46 tests passed\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
